it was in a remote compound in the high  desert of New Mexico that police found  the children 11 of them ranging in age  from 1 to 15 and in conditions police  say was shocking they apparently lived  in this partially buried trailer no  running water no plumbing no electricity  the only food a few potatoes and a box  of rice police say the children were  dirty and malnourished they were in bad  shape I mean the children were dirty  they didn't have clothes that fit them  properly just seen him walking around  like that it was it was it was hard to  see him during the search police  arrested this man suraj wa hodge who  they'd been tracking for weeks on  suspicion of abducting his own son in  december he wasn't among the children  rescued a second man Lukas Morton was  also arrested on suspicion of harboring  a fugitive three women believed to be  mothers of the children on the compound  were arrested but later released police  had moved in after being passed a  message from someone inside that people  were starving  it has shocked this small community this  people must be really sick to do  something like that to this kids it  scares me because it you know the safety  of my own children who are teenagers you  know you never know what can happen at  any given point america's seen these  stories before of course in january 13  children were found malnourished having  been allegedly held captive by their  parents at a house in california police  say it appears the children had been  living at this compound for a few months  but it's not known how they ended up  here they're now in the care of welfare  services authorities say their health  and safety is the number-one priority  Gregg Milam Sky News Los Angeles
 

